# MC-X-F12 (writer 9): charged's `at e` reads day_band, whose rows govern always: not law-dated, so the ask line
# reaching charged needs no law (L §4.3, an ask line: "unless that at itself reads something law-dated").
# day_band(3) = 10: at 2027-03-10, fee = 5.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input dom: int
input fee: money PLN
band day_band(a: int): int
def charged[m in months]: money PLN = fee at day_of(m, day_band(dom))
ask q: charged[2027-03]

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  day_band: [0, 15) = 10 "early"
  day_band: [15, 32) = 20 "late"

version v_f
  cite act
  governs 2027-01..2027-06
  known 2026-12-01
  dom = 3 governs always "dom"
  fee = 5.00 PLN "fee"
=== expect
q: 5.00 PLN
  cut 2027-12-31
